<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns pi ratings to 8 Japan chemical firms.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns pi ratings to 8 Japan chemical firms.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp (S&amp;P) said on Wednesday that it had assigned its 'pi' rating to eight Japanese chemical companies.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said in a statement that it viewed the credit profile of the industry as average or below average, reflecting its cyclical, commodity-like and capital-intensive nature.</p>
<p>S&amp;P's ratings of the eight companies are as follows:</p>
<p>    Asahi Chemical Industry Co Ltd	   Api</p>
<p>    Denki Kagaku Kogyo KK			BBpi</p>
<p>    Mitsubishi Chemical Corp		   BBBpi</p>
<p>    Mitsui Petrochemical Industries Ltd    BBBpi</p>
<p>    Shin-Etsu Chemical Co Ltd		  Api</p>
<p>    Showa Denko KK				 BBpi</p>
<p>    Sumitomo Chemical Co Ltd		   BBBpi</p>
<p>    Ube Industries Ltd			   BBpi</p>
</text>
